      "writtenOn": "2024-08-21T15:58:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We were given a list of ACPI device ids by Qualcomm that are available in the market, and we didn\u0027t see any correlation between ACPI ids and architectures. QC suggested to use hardcoded id instead to diverge code path if needed.\n\nThe approach you mentioned would require me to fill in the acpi vendor id for all vendors and it requires quite a bit of changes to the GPUInfo.cpp/.h template, which I am not confident enough to make those changes since I am not a frequent contributor. Since it is a cross-vendors changes, could we have someone from the Chromium side to take a look? This could be beneficial for future acpi devices of all vendors.\n\nBut yeah we do need this change ASAP to get pass some of the e2e failures.\n\n@rafael.cintron@microsoft.com Thought?",
